1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,425
The Value of Volunteering.

2
00:00:02,375 --> 00:00:06,550
Volunteering benefits the volunteer as much as the recipient.

3
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:13,925
Studies link regular volunteering with lower depression rates, better physical health, and greater life satisfaction.

4
00:00:13,925 --> 00:00:19,100
Helping others activates reward circuits in the brain and provides a sense of purpose.

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:23,125
Volunteering also builds skills and social connections.

6
00:00:23,125 --> 00:00:26,887
The type of volunteering matters less than consistency.

7
00:00:26,887 --> 00:00:30,500
A few hours monthly produces measurable benefits.

8
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:39,237
Starting with something aligned with one’s interests and values, with a commitment that feels sustainable rather than burdensome, yields the best results.

